mation of the New Avengers. 2006 \u2013 2007 (In-Universe) The Superhuman Registration Act is passed following the Stamford tragedy, sparking a Civil War between Iron Man and Captain America . The conflict ends with the surrender of Steve Rogers and his subsequent assassination. It fractured the hero community and led to the \"Dark Reign\" era where villains took control of national security. 2012 (In-Universe) The Phoenix Force returns to Earth in Avengers vs. X-Men, causing a war between the two factions over the fate of Hope Summers. Cyclops kills Charles Xavier while possessed by the Phoenix, fundamentally changing his character into a revolutionary figure. The event ended the \"No More Mutants\" era and reignited the mutant race. 2015 (In-Universe) The Multiverse is destroyed by Incursions, leading to the final Secret Wars. Doctor Doom uses the power of the Beyonders to create a new Battleworld, ruling as God Emperor until Reed Richards restores the Prime Marvel Universe (Earth-616). This served as a soft reboot that integrated characters like Miles Morales into the main continuity. 2019 (In-Universe) Charles Xavier, Magneto, and Moira MacTaggert establish a sovereign mutant nation on the living island of Krakoa. This \"House of X\" era introduces mutant resurrection protocols and a new isolationist foreign policy for mutantkind. It was the most radical status quo shift for the X-Men in thirty years. 2023 \u2013 2024 (In-Universe) The Fall of X sees the destruction of the Krakoan dream by the anti-mutant organization Orchis. This leads to the \"Rise of the Powers of X\" and the eventual transition into the \"From the Ashes\" era, where mutants return to living among humanity. This marked the end of the Krakoan age and a return to the classic \"outlaw\" status of the X-Men. May \u2013 August 2024 (Real-World) The Blood Hunt event, written by Jed MacKay, depicts a global vampire invasion led by Varnae, who possesses the body of Blade. The world is plunged into eternal darkness as the Avengers and Doctor Strange fight to reclaim the light. The event concludes with Doctor Doom becoming the Sorcerer Supreme after Stephen Strange abdicates his mantle to save the world. August \u2013 October 2024 (Real-World) The Venom War erupts as Eddie Brock and his son Dylan Brock fight for control over the Venom symbiote . Both have seen different futures where the other leads the world to ruin, leading to a massive conflict involving the \"Zombiotes.\" It redefines the relationship between the Brocks and the nature of the King in Black . Early 2025 (In-Universe) The \"One World Under Doom\" initiative begins, following Doctor Doom 's ascension to Sorcerer Supreme. Doom uses his combined mastery of science and magic to impose global order, forcing the Avengers into a role of underground resistance. This establishes Victor von Doom as the central antagonist and de facto ruler of the Marvel Universe heading into 2026. Overview The definitive guide to Marvel Comics, exploring its vast multiverse, iconic characters like Spider-Man and the Avengers, and its evolution from Timely Publications to a global cultural phenomenon. Characters A comprehensive guide to the definitive icons of the Marvel Comics universe, detailing the origins, powers, and interconnected relationships of Earth's Mightiest Heroes and their greatest adversaries. Deep Dive An exhaustive exploration of high-level Marvel Comics concepts, ranging from the metaphysical mechanics of the One-Above-All to the socio-political implications of the Krakoan Era and the structural integrity of the Multiversal Seventh and Eighth Firmaments. Creators A comprehensive guide to the architects of the Marvel Universe, featuring the foundational legends and the modern visionaries driving the 616 and Ultimate continuities into 2026. Controversies A comprehensive overview of production scandals, narrative retcons, and editorial shifts within Marvel Comics, ranging from the Silver Age to the modern e